  "source": {
    "title": "Portadown News, 18 January 1908, p. 5 (\"Portadown Municipal Election: Declaration of the Poll\")",
    "publisher": "Portadown News (via the British Newspaper Archive)",
    "kind": "news",
    "check": "every figure and the full names of the candidates read from the page image"
  },
  "note": "Triennial election of the whole council (fifteen seats, one area), Wednesday 15 January 1908, in the Town Hall; William Wilson was returning officer. Twenty-three were nominated, including twelve members of the retiring council. Anderson, R. Courtney, Gough, Wright, Wilson, White and W. J. Johnston were the nominees of the Orange Club. John Bell Bryson and Robert John Thornton tied on 502 for fifteenth place; Thornton offered to retire in Bryson's favour, but the returning officer was advised that a ballot was required, and Bryson's name was drawn first. The electorate, poll and spoiled papers are not given. No party labels printed."
}
